'''Koreasat 7''' (also known as '''Mugunghwa 7''') is a South Korean [[communications satellite]] operated by KT SAT, a subsidiary of [[KT Corporation]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://spacenews.com/40540kt-sat-picks-thales-alenia-over-orbital-sciences-for-two-satellite/|title=KT Sat Picks Thales Alenia over Orbital Sciences for Two-satellite Order|publisher=[[spacenews.com]]|date=12 May 2014|access-date=14 February 2018}}</ref> [[Thales Alenia Space]] was contracted in 2014 to build both it and [[Koreasat 5A]]. Koreasat 7A was launched into geosynchronous orbit on 4 May 2017 aboard an [[Ariane 5 ECA]] launch vehicle and placed at 116 degrees east longitude to provide coverage over [[East Asia]].<ref name="gunter">{{Cite web |last=Krebs |first=Gunter Dirk |title=Koreasat 7 (Mugunghwa 7) |url=https://space.skyrocket.de/doc_sdat/koreasat-7.htm |access-date=27 November 2022 |website=Gunter's Space Page}}</ref>

